<h2 id="h-what-to-add-to-an-rth-bow">What to Add to Any RTH Bow</h2>
<p>Even the best ready to hunt bow package leaves a few essentials to you:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>A release aid.</strong> A wrist-strap <?= amz('index finger bow release wrist strap', 'index finger release') ?> is the most common choice for new bowhunters.</li>
  <li><strong>Arrows matched to your setup.</strong> Spine depends on draw weight and draw length; a shop can help you choose.</li>
  <li><strong>A target.</strong> A <?= amz('archery bag target compound bow', 'bag target') ?> for field points and a foam block for broadhead practice.</li>
  <li><strong>A case.</strong> A padded <?= amz('compound bow case', 'compound bow case') ?> protects the sight and cams in the truck.</li>
</ul>

